## Module
`mrp_workorder` (enterprise), `quality_mrp_workorder` (enterprise)

## Version
19.0

## Steps to reproduce
1. Create and confirm a Manufacturing Order with quality checks (instruction or pass/fail type)
2. Open Shop Floor, navigate to the relevant work order
3. Complete an instruction check (click the checkmark) — line shows as crossed out with undo icon
4. Click the undo icon (fa-undo) — line reverts to uncompleted state ✓
5. **Refresh the page** (F5 / Ctrl+R)
6. The check shows as completed again (pass state) — the undo was not saved

## Expected behaviour
After clicking undo, the quality check `quality_state` should be written back to `"none"` in the database, so it persists across page reloads.

## Actual behaviour
The undo only mutates the client-side JavaScript object (`this.props.record.data.quality_state = "none"`) without any ORM call. The database retains `quality_state = "pass"`.

## Root cause

In `mrp_workorder/static/src/mrp_display/mrp_record_line/quality_check.js`:
```js
case "instructions":
    if (this.isComplete) {
        this.props.record.data.quality_state = "none";  // client-only, no ORM call
        return;
    }
```

In `quality_mrp_workorder/static/src/mrp_display/quality_check.js`:
```js
case "passfail":
    if (this.isComplete) {
        this.state.reOpened = true;
        this.props.record.data.quality_state = "none";  // client-only, no ORM call
        return;
    }
```

Note that `stock_move.js` handles undo correctly with a proper ORM call:
```js
async undo() {
    await this.props.record.model.orm.call(resModel, "action_undo", [[resId]]);
}
```

## Suggested fix

Add a server-side reset method and call it from both undo paths:

**Python** (`quality.check`):
```python
def action_undo(self):
    self.ensure_one()
    self.write({
        'quality_state': 'none',
        'user_id': False,
        'control_date': False,
    })
```

**JS** (both `quality_check.js` files):
```js
if (this.isComplete) {
    const { model, resModel, resId } = this.props.record;
    await model.orm.call(resModel, "action_undo", [resId]);
    this.props.record.data.quality_state = "none";
    return;
}
```

The pattern already exists in `stock_move.js` line 149-151 — just needs to be applied to the quality check undo paths as well.

